      "content": "but that's exactly what they want, right? that it's just \"alternative wellness\" so nobody takes it seriously. if you look at the history of how certain frequencies were standardized, it's never been purely about music or utility, it's always been about control. i've been tracking the subtle shifts in the hum from the local substation and it's definitely not a natural pattern. can you look into the technical specs of how the grid manages phase modulation? i want to see if there's any overlap between those industrial oscillations and the 440hz standard used to deaden cognitive function.",
